dient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="4"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">ground cinnamon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">0.04 oz</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">ground nutmeg</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">Wet Ingredients:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="7"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac34;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name"><a href="https://foolproofliving.com/how-to-make-almond-milk/" class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-link" target="_blank">almond milk</a></span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">unsweetened</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="8"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">maple syrup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">plus more for drizzling</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="9"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">large eggs at room temperature</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="10"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">vanilla extract</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="11"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">unsalted butter</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">or vegetable oil</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">Optional Toppings:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="13"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1/2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">mixed berries</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="14"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1/4</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">maple syrup</span></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-unit-conversion-container wprm-unit-conversion-container-23994 wprm-unit-conversion-container-links wprm-block-text-normal" style=""><a href="#" role="button" class="wprm-unit-conversion wprmpuc-active" data-system="1" data-recipe="23994" style="" aria-label="Change unit system to US Customary">US Customary</a> &ndash; <a href="#" role="button" class="wprm-unit-conversion" data-system="2" data-recipe="23994" style="" aria-label="Change unit system to Metric">Metric</a></div></div>
<div id="recipe-23994-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-23994-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="23994"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place almond flour, baking powder, kosher salt, ground cinnamon, and ground nutmeg in a medium mixing bowl. Whisk until well combined, breaking the large chunks of almond flour.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Almond-flour-pancake-mix-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Almond flour pancake mix batter in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Almond-flour-pancake-mix-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Almond-flour-pancake-mix-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Almond-flour-pancake-mix-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Almond-flour-pancake-mix.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Almond-flour-pancake-mix.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">In a separate, large mixing bowl, whisk together the almond milk, eggs, and vanilla extract until well incorporated.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add the dry ingredients to the wet ones and whisk until just combined, and you have a homogeneous batter.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Fluffy-almond-flour-pancakes-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing how to make pancakes with almond flour." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Fluffy-almond-flour-pancakes-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Fluffy-almond-flour-pancakes-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Fluffy-almond-flour-pancakes-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Fluffy-almond-flour-pancakes.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Fluffy-almond-flour-pancakes.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Heat a tablespoon of butter or vegetable oil in a 10-inch nonstick skillet over medium-low heat until it is melted.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Using a &frac14; cup measuring cup (approximately 2.54 oz/72 g.), scoop the batter into the skillet. Using a spatula, gently spread it to form a 3 &frac12;-inch circle. Continue with one more or as many as your pan will accommodate, but make sure not to crowd the skillet.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Let it cook for 4 minutes, and once it is lightly browned, flip and cook for another 4 minutes. Low and slow heat is the key here, so do not rush the process.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-6" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Transfer them to a plate and repeat the process with the remaining batter, using the remaining vegetable oil.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="248" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Gluten-free-pancakes-with-almond-flour-400x248.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="A collage of images showing how to cook and garnish almond pancakes." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Gluten-free-pancakes-with-almond-flour-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Gluten-free-pancakes-with-almond-flour-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Gluten-free-pancakes-with-almond-flour-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Gluten-free-pancakes-with-almond-flour.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Gluten-free-pancakes-with-almond-flour.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-23994-step-0-7" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When ready to serve, top it off with fresh berries and a drizzle of maple syrup.</div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-23994-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe yields 8 pancakes, serving 4. I weighed the ingredients using a kitchen scale while preparing the recipe. The nutritional values listed below are per pancake and do not include optional toppings.</li>
<li><strong>Paleo:&nbsp;</strong>If you are following a strict paleo diet, I recommend using a <a href="https://amzn.to/4mC5nTu" rel="nofollow">paleo-friendly baking powder</a>.&nbsp;</li>
<li><strong>Storage:</strong> Bring leftover pancakes to room temperature and store in an airtight container for up to 3 days.</li>
<li><strong>Freezing:&nbsp;</strong>Once they are fully cooled, place them in a freezer-safe container with small sheets of parchment paper (to prevent sticking) and remove as much air as possible. No need to thaw overnight. Take it out of the freezer 30 minutes before you are ready to serve.</li>
</ul></div></div>
